  push(P0(`ρ = max(*e*^{−κ}, ρ′) bounding the base of each of the three factors. By the triangle inequality *e*(*i*, *k*) ≥ *d*, and the number of pairs (*i*, *k*) with *e*(*i*, *k*) ≤ *n* is at most *N*(*f*)*N*(*g*)(2*n* + 1)^{8}, since *i* then lies within distance *n* of *S*(*f*) and *k* within distance *n* of *S*(*g*). Hence the last sum is at most *N*(*f*)*N*(*g*) Σ_{n≥d} (2*n* + 1)^{8} ρ^{n}, which is ρ^{d} times a polynomial in *d* and is therefore at most *K*₁ρ₁^{d} for every ρ₁ ∈ (ρ, 1), with *K*₁ depending on ρ, ρ₁, *N*(*f*) and *N*(*g*). Adding the second term gives the covariance inequality, with *K* = *K*′²*N*(*f*)*N*(*g*)‖*f*‖‖*g*‖*K*₁/(1 − α) + *K*′*N*(*f*)‖*f*‖‖*g*‖.`, { before: 0 }));
  push(P(`For the gap, let *f* be an observable, bounded uniformly in *j*, whose links lie in the time interval [0, *w*]. The links of θ*f̄* lie in [−*w*, 0] and those of τ_{t}*f* in [*t*, *t* + *w*]; the block boundaries in time are the multiples of *a*_{c} and a link belongs to the block of its midpoint, so *S*(θ*f̄*) lies in blocks of time index at most 0, *S*(τ_{t}*f*) in blocks of time index at least ⌊*t*/*a*_{c}⌋, and the distance between them is at least ⌊*t*/*a*_{c}⌋ ≥ *t*/*a*_{c} − 1. For *t* ∈ *D* and all large *j*, *t* is an integer multiple of *a*_{j}; the measure μ_{j} is invariant under the reflection θ and under the translation τ_{t}, so μ_{j}(θ*f̄*) is the complex conjugate of μ_{j}(*f*) and μ_{j}(τ_{t}*f*) = μ_{j}(*f*), and the covariance inequality gives *S*_{j}(θ*f̄* · τ_{t}*f*) − |*S*_{j}(*f*)|² ≤ (*K*/ρ₁)*e*^{−m₁t} with *m*₁ = log(1/ρ₁)/*a*_{c}, the constant independent of *j* and of the lattice because *N*(*f*) and ‖*f*‖ are. This is the hypothesis of Theorem 7.4 with *r*_{j} = 0 at every *t* ∈ *D*, so Theorem 7.4 leaves no spectrum in (0, *m*₁) for every ρ₁ ∈ (ρ, 1), hence none in (0, *m*), *m* = log(1/ρ)/*a*_{c}, the number of (8.8). ∎`, { before: 0 }));
  push(P(`Theorem 8.5′ contains Theorem 8.5 for every translation-covariant block map whose blocked measures have the form (S), which Theorem 8.5 itself does not need: under Hypotheses I and II and (S), the hypotheses of Theorem 8.5′ hold with the same constants, by Proposition 8.5E and the remark after Hypothesis II′, and its conclusion is the same, the factor 3 that the tilt by *G*′ puts into *K* in the proof of Theorem 8.5 being absent. Reflection positivity enters the proof only through Theorem 7.4, applied to the lattice measures μ_{j}; the blocked measure is not required to be reflection positive, and the step μ_{j}(θ*f̄*)μ_{j}(τ_{t}*f*) = |μ_{j}(*f*)|² uses the invariance of μ_{j} under θ and τ_{t} alone, not its positivity. The fibre clause enters only through the λ_{j}-mean of the fibre covariance and the L²(λ_{j}) local fluctuations of the fibre means; that is why its average suffices, and why the matrix of the coarse variables must be read in the same currency, Dobrushin's comparison theorem consuming the supremum oscillations δ_{y}.`));
